* Your microservice experiences long garbage-collection pauses. How would you investigate heap layout, allocation patterns, and the selected collector?
* Your application is slow immediately after startup but becomes faster later. How would you investigate interpretation, JIT compilation, and warm-up?
* Your production application has high CPU usage but no obvious application-level bottleneck. How would you investigate JIT compilation, garbage collection, thread activity, and native calls?
* A multithreaded service suffers from excessive thread creation and memory consumption. How would you assess thread stacks, platform threads, and virtual threads?
* Your service allocates many temporary objects and generates heavy garbage-collection activity. How would you investigate allocation behavior and possible JIT optimizations?
* Your application uses direct byte buffers and experiences native memory exhaustion. How would you distinguish heap usage from off-heap memory usage?
* A framework dynamically loads classes and creates proxies. How would you assess its effects on class metadata, class unloading, and Metaspace?
* Your application hangs during a garbage-collection event. How would you use thread dumps and JVM diagnostic tools to investigate thread states and safepoints?
* Your team needs to tune JVM memory for a container with a strict memory limit. How would you account for heap, Metaspace, thread stacks, direct memory, and other native allocations?
* Your service works correctly on one operating system but exhibits different memory behavior on another. How would you distinguish JVM specification guarantees from implementation-specific behavior?
* Your application has high latency and low throughput despite sufficient CPU and heap capacity. How would you investigate synchronization, thread contention, JIT behavior, and blocking operations?
